WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:03.640
Knitting socks in the round will eliminate

2
00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:08.000
a seam in the foot of your sock.
Before we get started,

3
00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:12.600
please be familiar with the settings for
knitting in the round on your machine.

4
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:17.640
You'll be slipping stitches on one bed
while knitting on the opposite bed.

5
00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:20.640
Also, you must swatch for your sock

6
00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:26.440
in the round. The gauge will differ
from knitting on the single bed.

7
00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:30.160
Start by casting on and
knitting your ribbing.

8
00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:34.000
Unless you want to hand-manipulate your
ribbing, you'll be knitting the rubbing

9
00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:39.200
flat and then switching
to circular knitting.

10
00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:47.320
When the ribbing is complete, transfer
all the stitches to the main bed.

11
00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.720
Drop the Ribber.

12
00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:02.200
Now you can knit one
plain row if you'd like.

13
00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:05.600
Put half of the stitches in hold

14
00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:11.120
and scrap off the other half.
Notice that I'm scrapping off opposite

15
00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:15.200
the carriage, the working yarn is
available for the next steps.

16
00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:18.440
This eliminates a yarn tail.

17
00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:33.840
Remove your cast on comb and weigths..

18
00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:49.360
Fold the scrapped edge and carefully rehang

19
00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:54.520
the stitches on the main bed,
doubling up the stitches.

20
00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:08.120
Remove the waste

21
00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:09.600
yarn.

22
00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:12.400
Add some weight.

23
00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:22.920
Raise your ribber and carefully transfer

24
00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:27.880
one stitch from each
needle down to the Ribber.

25
00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:38.960
Yes, this is tedious.

26
00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:42.080
There is no shortcut.

27
00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:05.840
And before you start knitting,

28
00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:10.000
carefully examine the stitches,
make sure that they're all picked up,

29
00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:15.680
no stitches have dropped
and none are crossing the beds.

30
00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:29.600
Set your carriages for circular knitting.
Slipping on one bed,

31
00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:33.480
knitting on the other,
and continue knitting in the round.

